{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Haryana in India (disputed hatched).svg|thumb|]]

===Etymology===
* Found in the works of the 1100s CE [[Apabhramsha]] writer Vibudh Shridhar.
* Derived from the Sanskrit words ''Hari'' (Vishnu) and ''ayana'' ("home"), meaning "the Abode of God".

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/hʌɹɪˈjɑːnə/|/hɑːɹɪˈjɑːnə/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-Haryana.wav|Audio (US)}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{place|en|state|in northern|c/India|capital=Chandigarh}}. [[Faridabad]] is its biggest city.

